c 4x5 grid graph minimum vertex cover instance (20 vertices, 31 edges, all weights 1).
c Vertices are numbered row by row: v(r, c) = 5*r + c + 1 for r in 0..3, c in 0..4.
c Encoding: variable v is true when vertex v is picked; hard (u v) per edge, soft (-v) weight 1.
c Optimal cost is 10: the grid is bipartite (checkerboard colouring), so by Konig's
c theorem the minimum vertex cover equals the maximum matching, and a 4x5 grid has a
c perfect matching of 10 edges. The solver returns 10, matching the theorem.
p wcnf 20 51 2
